# a difference between external and internal documentation is, external documentation is intended for users or stakeholders outside of the development team, while internal documentation is meant for developers and team members within the organization. External documentation focuses on providing instructions, guides, and information to help users understand and use the software effectively. Internal documentation, 
# on the other hand, includes technical details, code comments, and design specifications that aid developers in maintaining and enhancing the software. External documentation is 
# often more user-friendly and accessible, while internal documentation is more technical and detailed, catering to the needs of the development team.

# Yes we need to learn how to read and code documentation because, it is essential for understanding on how to work things properly and to solve problems.
# if we don't learn how to read and code documentation, we may struggle to understand how to use software, libraries, or frameworks effectively. This can lead to errors
# inefficiencies, and frustration when trying to implement features or troubleshoot issues.
# Additionally, without proper documentation skills, we may miss out on valuable insights and best practices that can enhance our coding abilities and overall development process

